# Website Defacement Monitor

A Python-based automated website defacement detection system that continuously monitors websites for unauthorized changes using visual hashing, DOM analysis, and behavioral signals. Runs as a Docker container with scheduled scan cycles and email alerting.

---

## Features

- Continuous monitoring with configurable scan intervals
- Baseline creation on first scan — only saved on HTTP 200 success
- Retry logic on failed scans — no false email alerts for downtime
- 20+ detection signals across visual, structural, and behavioral layers
- Site-type aware scoring — news/ecommerce sites scored differently from static sites
- Trusted domain whitelist — filters Google Analytics, live chat widgets, CDNs
- Comparison screenshots — side-by-side baseline vs latest scan
- Email alerts via SMTP with comparison image attached
- Dynamic domain list — edit `domains.txt` without restarting Docker
- JSON evidence output for each scan

---

## Requirements

- Docker and Docker Compose
- Gmail account with App Password (for email alerts)

---

## Project Structure

```
website-deface/
├── defacement_check.py     # Main monitor script
├── domains.txt             # List of URLs to monitor
├── .env                    # Configuration (never commit this)
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml
└── website_data/           # Auto-created on first run
    ├── baselines/          # JSON baseline snapshots
    ├── baseline_screenshots/
    ├── screenshots/        # Latest scan screenshots
    ├── comparisons/        # Side-by-side comparison images
    ├── evidence/           # Full JSON evidence per site
    ├── scan_results.json
    ├── suspicious.json
    └── likely_defaced.json
```

---

## Setup

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/youruser/website-deface-monitor.git
cd website-deface-monitor
```

### 2. Create your `.env` file

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Edit `.env`:

```env
# Scan interval in seconds (default: 300 = 5 minutes)
SCAN_INTERVAL_SECONDS=300

# Max parallel scans
MAX_CONCURRENT_SCANS=5

# Confidence threshold to send email alert (0-100)
ALERT_THRESHOLD=60

# Retry failed scans before giving up
MAX_SCAN_RETRIES=3
RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS=15

# SMTP email alerts (leave blank to disable)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USE_TLS=true
SMTP_USERNAME=you@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your_app_password
ALERT_EMAIL=alerts@you.com
```

> **Gmail setup:** Go to Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification → App Passwords. Generate a password for "Mail". Use that as `SMTP_PASSWORD`.

### 3. Add websites to monitor

Edit `domains.txt` — one URL per line. Optionally tag site type:

```
# Static sites — full visual scoring weight
https://example.com
https://gov.example.am

# News sites — reduced visual weight (content changes legitimately)
https://bbc.com  #type:news

# E-commerce — moderate visual weight
https://shop.example.com  #type:ecommerce
```

Supported types: `static` (default), `news`, `ecommerce`

> You can add or remove URLs at any time without restarting Docker. The list is re-read at the start of every scan cycle.

### 4. Build and run

```bash
docker compose build
docker compose up -d
```

### 5. Watch logs

```bash
docker compose logs -f
```

---

## How It Works

### Scan lifecycle

```
Cycle starts
    └── Load domains.txt (fresh read every cycle)
        └── For each URL (concurrent, up to MAX_CONCURRENT_SCANS):
            ├── No baseline exists?
            │   ├── Scan succeeds (HTTP 200) → Save baseline → Done
            │   └── Scan fails → Skip (try again next cycle)
            └── Baseline exists?
                ├── Scan succeeds → Compare → Score → Alert if >= threshold
                └── Scan fails → Retry up to MAX_SCAN_RETRIES times
                    ├── Eventually succeeds → Compare → Score → Alert if >= threshold
                    └── All retries fail → Create comparison image → NO email sent
Cycle ends → Sleep SCAN_INTERVAL_SECONDS → Repeat
```

### Detection signals

The monitor scores each site from 0–100%. Signals are grouped by category:

#### Visual
| Signal | Description |
|---|---|
| `MAJOR_VISUAL_CHANGE` | pHash distance ≥ 35 between screenshots |
| `MODERATE_VISUAL_CHANGE` | pHash distance ≥ 20 |
| `MINOR_VISUAL_CHANGE` | pHash distance ≥ 10 |
| `COLOR_SCHEME_REPLACED` | Brand color palette changed ≥ 80% |
| `COLOR_SCHEME_CHANGED` | Color palette changed ≥ 50% |

#### Identity
| Signal | Description |
|---|---|
| `IDENTITY_LOSS` | `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<footer>`, or logo disappeared |
| `MULTIPLE_IDENTITY_ELEMENTS_LOST` | 2+ identity elements gone |
| `LARGE_OVERLAY` | New large fixed-position element covering viewport |

#### Content
| Signal | Description |
|---|---|
| `TITLE_CHANGED` | Full page title replaced |
| `BRAND_PREFIX_CHANGED` | Brand name portion of title changed (strong signal even on news sites) |
| `LANGUAGE_SCRIPT_CHANGED` | Dominant text script changed (e.g. Latin → Armenian) |
| `META_DESCRIPTION_CHANGED` | Meta description changed (INFO only) |
| `DOM_STRUCTURE_CHANGED` | Structural DOM fingerprint changed (INFO only) |

#### Network
| Signal | Description |
|---|---|
| `NEW_EXTERNAL_DOMAINS` | New resource domains (non-whitelisted) |
| `NEW_SCRIPT_SRC_DOMAINS` | New `<script src="">` domains (non-whitelisted) |
| `NEW_IFRAME_EXTERNAL_SRC` | iframes now pointing to new external domains |
| `NAV_LINKS_NEW_DOMAINS` | Nav links now point to unknown external domains |
| `UNEXPECTED_DOMAIN_REDIRECT` | Final URL domain differs from baseline |
| `CANONICAL_DOMAIN_MISMATCH` | Canonical URL points to a different root domain |

#### Injection
| Signal | Description |
|---|---|
| `NEW_IFRAME` | New iframe elements appeared |
| `NEW_FORM` | New form elements appeared |
| `FORM_ACTION_EXFILTRATION` | Form posts to an external unknown domain |
| `ROBOTS_NOINDEX_INJECTED` | noindex meta tag appeared (attacker hiding page) |

#### Correlation bonuses
Combinations of signals trigger additional points:

| Correlation | Signals combined |
|---|---|
| `IDENTITY_VISUAL_CORRELATION` | Identity loss + visual change |
| `IDENTITY_OVERLAY_CORRELATION` | Identity loss + large overlay |
| `TITLE_DOMAIN_CORRELATION` | Title change + new external domains |
| `TITLE_VISUAL_CORRELATION` | Title change + visual change |
| `LANGUAGE_TITLE_CORRELATION` | Language change + title change |
| `BRAND_DOMAIN_CORRELATION` | Brand prefix change + new external domains |
| `FULL_REPLACEMENT_CORRELATION` | External domains + DOM change + visual change |
| `PHISHING_OVERLAY_CORRELATION` | Full overlay + form exfiltration |
| `CANONICAL_TITLE_CORRELATION` | Canonical hijack + title change |

### Verdict thresholds

| Confidence | Verdict |
|---|---|
| 90–100% | `VERY_LIKELY_DEFACED` |
| 70–89% | `LIKELY_DEFACED` |
| 40–69% | `SUSPICIOUS` |
| 0–39% | `LIKELY_NORMAL` |

Email is sent when confidence ≥ `ALERT_THRESHOLD` (default: 60%).

### Site types and visual scoring

Visual signals are multiplied by a weight based on site type to reduce false positives on dynamic sites:

| Type | Visual weight | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `static` | 1.0 (full) | Government, corporate, hospital sites |
| `ecommerce` | 0.5 | Online shops with changing product images |
| `news` | 0.3 | News portals where content changes every hour |

### Trusted domain whitelist

The following categories of domains are whitelisted and never contribute to scoring:

- **Google** — Analytics, Tag Manager, Fonts, Maps, Translate, reCAPTCHA
- **Cloudflare** — CDN, Insights
- **Social** — Facebook, Twitter, LinkedIn, Instagram
- **Live chat** — JivoSite, Tawk.to, OpenWidget, PureChat, ManyChat, Zendesk, Drift, Crisp
- **Marketing** — Scarab Research, Eventable, Eskimi, Snap (LinkedIn)
- **CDNs** — jsDelivr, unpkg, Bootstrap CDN, jQuery, DataTables, D3.js
- **Video** — YouTube, YouTube Privacy-enhanced, Vimeo
- **Analytics** — Hotjar, Yandex Metrica, New Relic, Segment, Mixpanel
- **Payments** — Stripe, PayPal
- **Other** — AddToAny, ShareThis, AddThis, Amazon S3/CloudFront, Gismeteo

---

## Output files

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `website_data/scan_results.json` | All sites from the latest cycle |
| `website_data/suspicious.json` | Sites scoring ≥ 40% |
| `website_data/likely_defaced.json` | Sites scoring ≥ 70% |
| `website_data/evidence/<site>.json` | Full snapshot + analysis per site |
| `website_data/comparisons/<site>_comparison.png` | Side-by-side screenshot |
| `website_data/baselines/<site>.json` | Stored baseline snapshot |
| `website_data/baseline_screenshots/<site>.png` | Baseline screenshot |

---

## Resetting a baseline

If a site legitimately redesigned and you want to re-baseline it:

```bash
# Reset one site
rm website_data/baselines/example_com.json
rm website_data/baseline_screenshots/example_com.png

# Reset all baselines
rm -rf website_data/baselines/ website_data/baseline_screenshots/
```

The next scan cycle will create a new baseline automatically.

---

## Full reset

```bash
docker compose down
rm -rf website_data/
docker compose up -d
```

---

## Environment variables reference

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `SCAN_INTERVAL_SECONDS` | `300` | Seconds between full scan cycles |
| `MAX_CONCURRENT_SCANS` | `5` | Max parallel browser tabs |
| `ALERT_THRESHOLD` | `60` | Min confidence % to send email |
| `MAX_SCAN_RETRIES` | `3` | Retries on scan failure |
| `RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS` | `15` | Seconds between retries |
| `SMTP_HOST` | `smtp.gmail.com` | SMTP server |
| `SMTP_PORT` | `587` | SMTP port |
| `SMTP_USE_TLS` | `true` | Use STARTTLS |
| `SMTP_USERNAME` | | Your email address |
| `SMTP_PASSWORD` | | App password |
| `ALERT_EMAIL` | | Alert recipient |

---

## .env.example

```env
SCAN_INTERVAL_SECONDS=300
MAX_CONCURRENT_SCANS=5
ALERT_THRESHOLD=60
MAX_SCAN_RETRIES=3
RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS=15

SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USE_TLS=true
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
ALERT_EMAIL=
```

---

## Security notes

- Never commit `.env` to version control — it contains your email credentials
- Add `.env` to `.gitignore`
- The monitor uses a headless Chromium browser — keep the Docker image updated
- Baselines are stored as plaintext JSON — keep the `website_data/` directory access-controlled

